* ''The vessel reads its own durability'' (operator, 2026-11-06, approving the house's defaults). The vessel reads its own storage durability (`persisted()`, the storage class) and names erasable storage before a founding or a join binds; a wiped keystore boots as a new vessel, by name. Safari's seven-day rule rides as a measured platform condition, dated and sourced, never as an evergreen constant, and a granted persistence request guarantees nothing beyond what the platform reports. Carrier: `pono/browser-vessel-lift`, slice 7, carried by the b1 lanes' carriers at their land.

